* RENAME - CHANGE A FILE NAME

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* RENAME - CHANGE A FILE NAME

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:RENAME newname=oldname

Renames an existing file without copying its contents. Example:
SYSUTLS:RENAME I0:NEW.TXT=I0:OLD.TXT

Both names must refer to the same drive; do not use this as a move between
disks. Check the new name and any overwrite prompt. Changing a COM
filename can change command lookup and startup behavior.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
